  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $4:8$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($8$).\n\nWe can make a numerator of $12$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\times 3}{8\\times 3} & =\\frac{12}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $24$ |\n| $20$ | $40$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $24.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
